# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage

# The rendered site. Not committed on purpose: every number it publishes lives in
# docs/data/catalogue.json, which is committed and gated in CI, so a change to a
# published number is already a diff. Committing the render would add a 500-page
# diff to every template change and one more staleness gate to satisfy.
/site/

# The fetched reports. 90 MB of archives that unpack to 450 MB of HTML, produced
# by genomic-benchmarks-qc and published on Zenodo. `data/reports.csv` carries the
# manifest -- name, size, digest, every path inside -- so what is missing here is
# still describable, and `gb-audit fetch` brings it back verified.
/docs/reports/

# NOT a pattern for `docs/templates/parts/`. A bare `parts/` here -- which the
# usual Python .gitignore ships, for setuptools' build output -- has no leading
# slash, so git applies it at every depth and silently swallows the eleven prose
# fragments the site is assembled from. That happened once already in the
# leaderboard repository. If setuptools' `parts/` is ever needed, anchor it.
/parts/

# Editors and platforms
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
